16 0 obj
<</A 60 0 R/Alt(Two panels show tomato plants in different stages. Panel \(a\) captures close-ups of various tomatoes ranging from green to ripe red on vines. Panel \(b\) displays wider views of tomato plants with clusters of tomatoes under broad green leaves in a greenhouse setting.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 41 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

17 0 obj
<</A 61 0 R/Alt(A series of tomato leaves showing different conditions. Top row: healthy leaf, early blight with brown spots, late blight with extensive darkening, and yellowing leaf mold. Bottom row: healthy leaf, early blight, late blight, leaf mold, target spot with brown lesions, and black spot with darkened areas.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 42 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

18 0 obj
<</A 62 0 R/Alt(\(a\) A ZED stereo camera featuring two lenses for depth perception, housed in a sleek black and silver case. \(b\) A compact computing board with a small fan, various ports, and connectors on a black circuit board. \(c\) A robotic platform with a mounted computing board, motors, and wheels, arranged on a tiled floor.)/K 1/P 8 0 R/Pg 42 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

19 0 obj
<</A 63 0 R/Alt(Diagram of a tomato maturity detection system using deep learning. Various hardware components are shown: a binocular camera, a GPU, and mobile devices. The system architecture includes GhostConv and E-IoU modules. The flow from input to detection results is depicted, showcasing the integration of improved network layers. On the right, software screenshots display disease detection, focusing on black spot disease, with suggestion text and detection results. An arrow indicates the process flow from detection results to integrated software through a revised LLM module.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 43 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

20 0 obj
<</A 64 0 R/Alt(Flowchart detailing a complex neural network architecture for object detection. It includes components like GhostConv, C3K2, MaxPool2d, BottleNeck, and PSABlock. The structure is divided into sections: Backbone, SPPF, C3K2, Neck, and Head. Arrows illustrate data flow, with input leading through layers to detection output in red boxes labeled \215Detect.\216 Sub-diagrams at the bottom provide identity transformation and box dimension details.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 44 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

21 0 obj
<</A 65 0 R/Alt<>/K 1/P 8 0 R/Pg 44 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

22 0 obj
<</A 66 0 R/Alt<>/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 45 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

23 0 obj
<</A 67 0 R/Alt(Diagram illustrating three boxes: a green anchor box \(A\), a black target box \(B\), and a blue dashed minimum enclosing box \(C\). Central points are marked as \\\(b\\\) and \\\(b^{gt}\\\). Dimensions are labeled as \\\(w\\\), \\\(h\\\), \\\(w^{gt}\\\), \\\(h^{gt}\\\), \\\(w^{c}\\\), and \\\(h^{c}\\\). A legend explains the symbols.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 46 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

24 0 obj
<</A 68 0 R/Alt(Two line graphs compare neural network models. Graph \(a\) plots accuracy against FLOPs, showing GhostNet and MobileNetV3 with highest accuracy increases. Graph \(b\) plots accuracy against latency, with GhostNet again leading. Legend identifies models using different colors and line styles.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 50 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

25 0 obj
<</A 69 0 R/Alt(Grid of six line charts showing training and validation losses and metrics over epochs. Training loss charts are for box, class, and DFL losses, all decreasing. Validation loss charts similarly decrease. Precision, recall, mAP50, and mAP50-95 metrics charts generally increase, showing performance improvement.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 52 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

26 0 obj
<</A 70 0 R/Alt(Multiple images of tomato plants and tomatoes. Group \(a\) shows close-up images of tomatoes and plants with blue boxes and confidence scores indicating detection. Group \(b\) displays a larger view of tomatoes growing on vines with similar annotations. The confidence scores vary, displayed in blue text, suggesting automated recognition in a computer vision context.)/K 1/P 8 0 R/Pg 52 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

27 0 obj
<</A 71 0 R/Alt(A series of images showing leaves with varying disease annotations. Panel \(a\) displays leaves with labels indicating \215Early Blight\216 and \215Healthy,\216 with confidence scores. Panel \(b\) shows leaves marked with \215Leaf Mold,\216 \215Early Blight,\216 and \215Black Spot,\216 each with associated confidence scores. Panel \(c\) has similar annotations with \215Early Blight,\216 \215Leaf Mold,\216 and \215Black Spot,\216 also including confidence values. The images demonstrate the detection of different leaf diseases using bounding boxes and color-coded labels.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 54 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

28 0 obj
<</A 72 0 R/Alt(Normalized confusion matrix showing classification accuracy for various plant diseases. The diagonal shows high accuracy for Healthy \(1.00\), Early Blight \(0.83\), and Target Spot \(0.67\). Off-diagonal values indicate classification errors, with lighter shades representing lower accuracy. A color bar on the right visually represents accuracy levels from 0.0 to 1.0.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 55 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

29 0 obj
<</A 73 0 R/Alt(Confusion matrix for tomato ripeness classification showing predicted versus true labels: Immature \(26 true positive, 3 false positive\), Ripe \(88 true positive, 4 false negative\), Overripe \(4 true positive, 1 false negative\). Overall accuracy is 92.91 percent. Precision, recall, and F1 scores are detailed for each class: Immature \(0.87, 0.90, 0.88\), Ripe \(0.80, 0.80, 0.80\), Overripe \(0.96, 0.95, 0.95\). Color scale indicates frequency.)/K 1/P 8 0 R/Pg 55 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

30 0 obj
<</A 74 0 R/Alt(Graph \(a\) shows a scatter plot of true versus predicted tomato counts using an improved YOLO model. A red dashed line indicates perfect predictions. Evaluation metrics are: mean absolute error 1.13, mean squared error 1.93, and R-squared 0.71. Graph \(b\) displays a bar chart of prediction errors: frequency versus prediction error. Error statistics include mean error -0.60, standard deviation 1.25, maximum overestimate 2.0, and maximum underestimate -2.0. A red dashed line indicates zero error.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 56 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

31 0 obj
<</A 75 0 R/Alt(Tomato Maturity Detection System interface with two panels. Panel \(a\) displays images of tomatoes on a vine labeled for maturity with a confidence rating of 0.98. Detection data includes image file paths, classification as mature, and positioning coordinates. Panel \(b\) shows a tomato leaf diagnosed with leaf mold, indicated within the image. Text provides prevention measures for leaf diseases, such as proper sanitation, spacing plants, mulching, and using resistant varieties. Both panels are part of a deep learning system for plant health monitoring.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 57 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

